    "turn_text": "Well, you would think so, but again, the NIH Acting Director just last week in committee, when I asked the question, said no, that there was no funding for that. So there are definitely conflicting things here. I think Dr. Fauci or Mr. Fauci himself even admitted that there was money that went to a sub-grant from EcoHealth to the Wuhan Institute of Virology. And so that's why our committee And Comer signed on to the letter and Dr. Winstrup, who's the chair of the subcommittee and myself. And we asked Dr. Fauci, Peter Dasik, who's the president of EcoHealth Alliance and the director of national intelligence. And the Francis Collins, who now works for the president, but was the former NIH director and secretary of HHS, Versera. We ask them for documents, communications, calendar notes, we want testimony, we want interviews, we want to interview 29 HHS officials. And so this is, we asked for this information when we were in the minority and now that we're in the majority, we ask for it again and we expect that we'll get the answers. We'll find out, won't we?",
