    "turn_text": "So I mean, I can't come up with the three fifty to five hundred dollars to fill up a sessna. So no, it's part. But anyway, what I called you about was this. When you fly privately, and of course, commercially, you have something on board called a transponder. That transponder is sending a signal to an air traffic controller. With that, the air traffic controller has your tail number, and they know what altitude you're flying. These balloons, if they don't have electronic film board, they are not required to have a transponder. But if they do have electronic film board, they are required to have one, or if they fly above 18,000 feet, I think it is. Okay, I'm starting to wonder, and I heard Man yesterday on your show who's down at almost hysterical, that we're being told that they have no idea what these balloons are don't believe that for one second i don't",
